              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for an explanation, then the Marathi for to come about."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मुद्दा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुद्दा — muddā — \"a point at issue; a point in an argument\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हा मुद्दा फार महत्त्वाचा आहे. hā muddā phār mahattvācā āhe. This point is very important."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. Plural: मुद्दे, mudde."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुद्द्यावर येणे, to come to the point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुद्दा (muddā) is a loan from Persian, usually traced to Arabic muddaʿā, \"a thing claimed or alleged\", from the same Arabic root as daʿwā, \"a claim\"; in Marathi it is the point under discussion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
